From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:15:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] platform/surface: platform_profile: Start the X2 Surfaces
 with a fan at balanced

The Surface Pro 12th Edition and the Surface Laptop 13in 2nd Edition
have the Surface Laptop 8's fan (FAN0) and SAM thermal profile. Treat
their EC as the Surface Laptop 8's: if it reports profile 0, start from
balanced. An EC that reports its profile is left as it is.

Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
---
 drivers/platform/surface/surface_platform_profile.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/platform/surface/surface_platform_profile.c b/drivers/platform/surface/surface_platform_profile.c
index c2b01f0..0b25750 100644
--- a/drivers/platform/surface/surface_platform_profile.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/surface/surface_platform_profile.c
@@ -247,7 +247,9 @@ static int surface_platform_profile_probe(struct ssam_device *sdev)
 
 	tpd->has_fan = device_property_read_bool(&sdev->dev, "has_fan");
 	tpd->ec_reports_zero = of_machine_is_compatible("microsoft,surface-laptop-8-13p8") ||
-			       of_machine_is_compatible("microsoft,surface-laptop-8-15");
+			       of_machine_is_compatible("microsoft,surface-laptop-8-15") ||
+			       of_machine_is_compatible("microsoft,surface-laptop-13in-2nd-edition") ||
+			       of_machine_is_compatible("microsoft,surface-pro-12th-edition");
 
 	/*
 	 * If the EC does not report its profile, start from a known one:
